   "text": {
    "L1": "In the hot summer, the pond dries up, and Dhruv is too tired to walk to the far river.",
    "L2": "A little monkey helps him by shaking the berry tree, so berries fall near him.",
    "L3": "The elephant is kind because she brings cool water from the river for Dhruv to drink.",
    "L4": "Dhruv is wise because he remembers a hidden spring and shows it to everyone.",
    "L5": "Here is the myth: spring always means the season. That is not true.",
    "L6": "In one sentence, spring means the season. In another, it means water coming out of the ground.",
    "L7": "Use an before a vowel sound: an elephant and an old stag. Use a before a consonant sound: a monkey.",
    "L8": "The lesson is simple: when we are kind to others, kindness comes back and everyone is helped."
   },
